# BuildKit looks for <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile
# before falling back to the context-wide .dockerignore. That fallback is what
# this file exists to avoid: .dockerignore excludes models/, which is right for
# the application image and wrong here - against the ./backend context,
# `COPY models /models` then fails the build with `"/models": not found`.
#
# Note this file REPLACES backend/.dockerignore for this build; it does not add
# to it. Everything that file denies by name - training/, .env, the caches - is
# covered here only by the blanket `*`, so the deny block at the end restates
# the two that matter most.
#
# Docker applies last match wins, which is exactly why the deny block sits at
# the bottom: it beats every `!` above it, and it does NOT beat one appended
# below it - which is where a person naturally adds a pattern. Any new `!` line
# belongs above the deny block, and must be checked against
# backend/.dockerignore's deny list first. This image is published.
#
# In normal use scripts/build_model_image.sh builds against a staged context
# holding only allowlisted model files, so `*` has little left to exclude. This
# file is the second line of defence, for a build run against ./backend by hand.
*
!models
training/
.env
